        "tree_id": "a2f8f3a87fb1863cb941d7e5e129a900074a9d39",
        "message": "feat(PR-N3): zero-sum minor-unit ledger and crash-safe restore\n\nMoney is bigint minor units only (D150): one entry moves a positive amount\nfrom debit to credit, so the signed sum over all accounts is zero by\nconstruction. Idempotency keys map to FNV-1a payload hashes: an identical\nreplay returns duplicate, a changed payload raises conflict, never an\noverwrite. System accounts are explicit ids (mint, burn, fees).\n\nA checkpoint is a plain object with balances, applied keys, an ordered log\nand a checksum. Restore replays the log and hard-fails on any balance, key\nor checksum mismatch — it never silently repairs.\n\nThe fuzz posts 10 000 transactions, dedupes 1000 reverse-ordered replays,\nraises one conflict, ends at drift 0 minor units, and posts 0 transactions\nafter crash restore. Local structural run only: no database, no concurrency,\nno disk benchmark, no RPO promise.\n\nGDD-PERSISTENCE 0.3 and GDD-TRADE 0.3 (I9); both corrupted §18 tables\nrepaired. PR-N3 acc repaired to a real vitest command (ninth broken form).\nB2 caught the prototype report's ownership: qa-engineer added as co-owner.\n\nAcceptance: fuzz 7/7, core 41/41, full 132/132, verify 17/17, tracer green.\n\nAgent: backend-engineer\nTask: PR-N3",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:30:42Z",
